From 6e67f03cbbc1bdc2339bdfeeae018ff25bf428d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:10:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/71] kbuild: Track an empty .scmversion so the release stays
 4.14.190-perf

This tree is a git repository, so scripts/setlocalversion appends "+" and the
kernel release becomes 4.14.190-perf+, which no longer matches the vendor DLKM
vermagic ("4.14.190-perf SMP preempt mod_unload modversions aarch64"): every
module in /vendor/lib/modules is then rejected.  An empty .scmversion keeps the
release exact.  The top-level .gitignore ignores dotfiles, so un-ignore it and
add it explicitly.

Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .gitignore  | 3 +++
 .scmversion | 0
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 .scmversion

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 2eb11afdf..dfc28cf9a 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -132,3 +132,6 @@ kernel/configs/android-*.cfg
 Android.bp
 out/
 out_*/
+
+# keep the kernel release pinned to 4.14.190-perf
+!.scmversion
diff --git a/.scmversion b/.scmversion
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..e69de29bb
